('TFW-20261009-01','2026-10-09',('2026-10-29 20:00'::timestamp at time zone 'America/Toronto'),'Carousel','CAROUSEL',$c$2026-10-09_Carousel_TEF-Section-A-Phone-Call$c$,'2026-10-09_Carousel_TEF-Section-A-Phone-Call',array['https://raw.githubusercontent.com/thefrenchway2pr-ux/tfw2pr-media/main/media/2026-10-09/2026-10-09_Carousel_TEF-Section-A-Phone-Call_01.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/thefrenchway2pr-ux/tfw2pr-media/main/media/2026-10-09/2026-10-09_Carousel_TEF-Section-A-Phone-Call_02.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/thefrenchway2pr-ux/tfw2pr-media/main/media/2026-10-09/2026-10-09_Carousel_TEF-Section-A-Phone-Call_03.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/thefrenchway2pr-ux/tfw2pr-media/main/media/2026-10-09/2026-10-09_Carousel_TEF-Section-A-Phone-Call_04.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/thefrenchway2pr-ux/tfw2pr-media/main/media/2026-10-09/2026-10-09_Carousel_TEF-Section-A-Phone-Call_05.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/thefrenchway2pr-ux/tfw2pr-media/main/media/2026-10-09/2026-10-09_Carousel_TEF-Section-A-Phone-Call_06.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/thefrenchway2pr-ux/tfw2pr-media/main/media/2026-10-09/2026-10-09_Carousel_TEF-Section-A-Phone-Call_07.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/thefrenchway2pr-ux/tfw2pr-media/main/media/2026-10-09/2026-10-09_Carousel_TEF-Section-A-Phone-Call_08.jpg'],$c$If you run out of questions after three, this one's for you. In TEF Canada oral Section A, you get an ad and about 5 minutes to call and ask for information.

The method in 4 steps (swipe for the full breakdown):
1. Open like a real phone call
2. Vary your question forms
3. Soften with the conditionnel
4. React before your next question

10 questions you can adapt to almost any ad:
→ Est-ce que le chauffage est inclus ? (Is heating included?)
→ Combien coûte le stationnement ? (How much is parking?)
→ À quel étage se trouve l'appartement ? (What floor is it on?)
→ Quand est-ce que le bail commence ? (When does the lease start?)
→ Les animaux sont-ils acceptés ? (Are pets allowed?)
→ Est-ce qu'il y a une laveuse et une sécheuse ? (Is there a washer and dryer?)
→ Je voudrais savoir si l'appartement est meublé. (I'd like to know if it's furnished.)
→ Pourriez-vous me décrire le quartier ? (Could you describe the neighborhood?)
→ Serait-il possible de visiter samedi ? (Would it be possible to visit on Saturday?)
→ Pardon, pouvez-vous répéter le prix ? (Sorry, can you repeat the price?)

Takeaway: mix « Est-ce que », question words and inversion, and react to each answer (« D'accord, donc… »). That turns a list of questions into a conversation. TCF Canada speaking Task 2 works the same way.

Quiz answers (slide 7): 1. Est-ce que · 2. Combien · 3. si

Want 3 full practice calls and 10 exercises? DM « PR » and I'll send you the practical guide.

