('TFW-20261011-01','2026-10-11',('2026-10-31 20:00'::timestamp at time zone 'America/Toronto'),'Carousel','CAROUSEL',$c$2026-10-11_Carousel_Story-Un-Bruit-au-Sous-Sol$c$,'2026-10-11_Carousel_Story-Un-Bruit-au-Sous-Sol',array['https://raw.githubusercontent.com/thefrenchway2pr-ux/tfw2pr-media/main/media/2026-10-11/2026-10-11_Carousel_Story-Un-Bruit-au-Sous-Sol_01.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/thefrenchway2pr-ux/tfw2pr-media/main/media/2026-10-11/2026-10-11_Carousel_Story-Un-Bruit-au-Sous-Sol_02.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/thefrenchway2pr-ux/tfw2pr-media/main/media/2026-10-11/2026-10-11_Carousel_Story-Un-Bruit-au-Sous-Sol_03.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/thefrenchway2pr-ux/tfw2pr-media/main/media/2026-10-11/2026-10-11_Carousel_Story-Un-Bruit-au-Sous-Sol_04.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/thefrenchway2pr-ux/tfw2pr-media/main/media/2026-10-11/2026-10-11_Carousel_Story-Un-Bruit-au-Sous-Sol_05.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/thefrenchway2pr-ux/tfw2pr-media/main/media/2026-10-11/2026-10-11_Carousel_Story-Un-Bruit-au-Sous-Sol_06.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/thefrenchway2pr-ux/tfw2pr-media/main/media/2026-10-11/2026-10-11_Carousel_Story-Un-Bruit-au-Sous-Sol_07.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/thefrenchway2pr-ux/tfw2pr-media/main/media/2026-10-11/2026-10-11_Carousel_Story-Un-Bruit-au-Sous-Sol_08.jpg'],$c$Midnight. Snow outside. A strange BEEP from the basement… Can you follow a suspense story in French at A1? Let's find out.

This mini story is written like the stories in our A1 suspense reader: short sentences, present tense, and everyday words you'll reuse all the time in Canada. Swipe, read each part out loud, then answer the 3 questions on slide 7.

10 words from the story:
→ minuit (midnight)
→ soudain (suddenly)
→ un bruit (a noise)
→ le sous-sol (the basement)
→ avoir peur (to be scared): « J'ai peur », never « Je suis peur »
→ descendre l'escalier (to go down the stairs)
→ il fait noir (it's dark)
→ allumer (to switch on). Opposite: éteindre
→ clignoter (to blink)
→ le linge (laundry)

Takeaway: after reading, close the app and retell the story in 3 sentences out loud. Retelling is how reading turns into speaking.

Answers (no peeking!):
1. Priya habite à Montréal (dans un appartement).
2. Le bruit vient du sous-sol.
3. C'est la sécheuse ! It beeps and blinks when the cycle is finished, and Priya forgot her laundry.

Did you guess the ending? Comment your 3 answers in French below. I reply to every one.

