insert into public.social_posts (row_id,post_date,publish_at,content_type,ig_media_type,topic,asset_name,media_urls,caption,alt_text,approved,status,notes) values
('TFW-20261012-01','2026-10-12',('2026-11-01 20:00'::timestamp at time zone 'America/Toronto'),'Static','IMAGE',$c$2026-10-12_Static_Passe-Compose-Etre$c$,'2026-10-12_Static_Passe-Compose-Etre',array['https://raw.githubusercontent.com/thefrenchway2pr-ux/tfw2pr-media/main/media/2026-10-12/2026-10-12_Static_Passe-Compose-Etre_01.jpg'],$c$« J'ai allé au travail. » If you've said this, you're in good company. It's one of the most common mistakes we hear, and it's an easy fix.

In the passé composé, most verbs use avoir. A short list of movement and change-of-state verbs uses être, and so does every reflexive verb. With être, the past participle agrees with the subject: add -e for a woman, -s for plural.

10 examples with être:
→ Je suis allé(e) au bureau. (I went to the office.)
→ Je suis arrivé(e) au Canada en 2024. (I arrived in Canada in 2024.)
→ Elle est partie à 17 h. (She left at 5 p.m.)
→ Il est né à Chandigarh. (He was born in Chandigarh.)
→ Nous sommes resté(e)s à la maison. (We stayed home.)
→ Ils sont venus à la réunion. (They came to the meeting.)
→ Elle est tombée sur le trottoir glacé. (She fell on the icy sidewalk.)
→ Je suis rentré(e) tard. (I got home late.)
→ Il est devenu gestionnaire. (He became a manager.)
→ Je me suis inscrit(e) au cours. (I signed up for the class.) Reflexive → être.

Watch out: with a direct object, sortir, monter, descendre, rentrer, retourner and passer switch to avoir. J'ai sorti les poubelles. (I took out the garbage.)

Takeaway: before you say a past sentence, ask yourself: is this movement, a change of state, or a reflexive verb? If yes, use être. If not, use avoir.

Want 3 real conversations (office, clinic, job interview) and 10 exercises with answers? DM « PR » and I'll send you the practical guide.

