('TFW-20261018-01','2026-10-18',('2026-11-06 20:00'::timestamp at time zone 'America/Toronto'),'Carousel','CAROUSEL',$c$2026-10-18_Carousel_Story-Le-Dernier-Autobus$c$,'2026-10-18_Carousel_Story-Le-Dernier-Autobus',array['https://raw.githubusercontent.com/thefrenchway2pr-ux/tfw2pr-media/main/media/2026-10-18/2026-10-18_Carousel_Story-Le-Dernier-Autobus_01.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/thefrenchway2pr-ux/tfw2pr-media/main/media/2026-10-18/2026-10-18_Carousel_Story-Le-Dernier-Autobus_02.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/thefrenchway2pr-ux/tfw2pr-media/main/media/2026-10-18/2026-10-18_Carousel_Story-Le-Dernier-Autobus_03.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/thefrenchway2pr-ux/tfw2pr-media/main/media/2026-10-18/2026-10-18_Carousel_Story-Le-Dernier-Autobus_04.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/thefrenchway2pr-ux/tfw2pr-media/main/media/2026-10-18/2026-10-18_Carousel_Story-Le-Dernier-Autobus_05.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/thefrenchway2pr-ux/tfw2pr-media/main/media/2026-10-18/2026-10-18_Carousel_Story-Le-Dernier-Autobus_06.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/thefrenchway2pr-ux/tfw2pr-media/main/media/2026-10-18/2026-10-18_Carousel_Story-Le-Dernier-Autobus_07.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/thefrenchway2pr-ux/tfw2pr-media/main/media/2026-10-18/2026-10-18_Carousel_Story-Le-Dernier-Autobus_08.jpg'],$c$11 p.m. The last bus. A man in a black coat gets off at your stop… and walks right behind you. Can you follow this suspense story in French? It's A1.

This mini story is written like the stories in our A1 suspense reader: short sentences, the present tense, and words you'll use on every bus ride in Canada. Swipe, read each part out loud, then answer the 3 questions on slide 7.

10 words from the story:
→ le dernier autobus (the last bus)
→ un arrêt d'autobus (a bus stop)
→ monter / descendre (to get on / to get off)
→ au fond (at the back)
→ derrière (behind). Opposite: devant (in front of)
→ suivre: il me suit (to follow: he's following me)
→ marcher vite (to walk fast)
→ mon cœur bat fort (my heart is pounding)
→ se retourner (to turn around)
→ le portefeuille (the wallet)

Takeaway: learn new words in pairs. Monter / descendre, derrière / devant, vite / lentement. When you remember one, the other comes with it.

Answers (no peeking):
1. À 23 h (11 p.m.).
2. Derrière Arjun.
3. Son portefeuille ! It fell on the bus, and the man ran after Arjun to give it back.

Did you guess the ending? Comment your 3 answers in French below. I reply to every one.

