insert into public.social_posts (row_id,post_date,publish_at,content_type,ig_media_type,topic,asset_name,media_urls,caption,alt_text,approved,status,notes) values
('TFW-20261022-01','2026-10-22',('2026-11-10 20:00'::timestamp at time zone 'America/Toronto'),'Carousel','CAROUSEL',$c$2026-10-22_Carousel_Renting-an-Apartment$c$,'2026-10-22_Carousel_Renting-an-Apartment',array['https://raw.githubusercontent.com/thefrenchway2pr-ux/tfw2pr-media/main/media/2026-10-22/2026-10-22_Carousel_Renting-an-Apartment_01.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/thefrenchway2pr-ux/tfw2pr-media/main/media/2026-10-22/2026-10-22_Carousel_Renting-an-Apartment_02.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/thefrenchway2pr-ux/tfw2pr-media/main/media/2026-10-22/2026-10-22_Carousel_Renting-an-Apartment_03.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/thefrenchway2pr-ux/tfw2pr-media/main/media/2026-10-22/2026-10-22_Carousel_Renting-an-Apartment_04.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/thefrenchway2pr-ux/tfw2pr-media/main/media/2026-10-22/2026-10-22_Carousel_Renting-an-Apartment_05.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/thefrenchway2pr-ux/tfw2pr-media/main/media/2026-10-22/2026-10-22_Carousel_Renting-an-Apartment_06.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/thefrenchway2pr-ux/tfw2pr-media/main/media/2026-10-22/2026-10-22_Carousel_Renting-an-Apartment_07.jpg'],$c$« 3 ½ à louer, chauffé, éclairé, libre le 1er juillet. » If you're looking for an apartment in Québec, ads look like this. Here's how to read them, and what to say when you call.

Renting in French comes down to four moments: reading the ad, contacting the landlord, asking questions at the visit, and reporting a problem. Swipe for 5 phrases for each.

10 to save:
→ un 3 ½ (a one-bedroom apartment in Québec: kitchen, living room, bedroom + the bathroom as ½)
→ chauffé, éclairé (heat and electricity included)
→ entrées laveuse-sécheuse (washer-dryer hookups)
→ Est-ce qu'il est toujours disponible ? (Is it still available?)
→ Je pourrais le visiter cette semaine ? (Could I see it this week?)
→ Le loyer est de combien par mois ? (How much is the rent per month?)
→ Est-ce que le chauffage est inclus ? (Is heating included?)
→ C'est un bail d'un an ? (Is it a one-year lease?) Le bail = the lease, le loyer = the rent.
→ Le chauffage ne fonctionne pas. (The heating isn't working.)
→ Pouvez-vous envoyer quelqu'un ? (Can you send someone?)

Takeaway: use vous with a landlord, and « Je pourrais… » to sound polite. In everyday speech, a rising voice turns a sentence into a question: « Le chauffage est inclus ? »

Quiz answers (slide 6): 1. inclus · 2. visiter · 3. fuite

Reading these is easy. Saying them on the phone when the landlord talks fast is the hard part, and that's what we practice out loud in our small classes. Book a trial class: link in bio.

