insert into public.social_posts (row_id,post_date,publish_at,content_type,ig_media_type,topic,asset_name,media_urls,caption,alt_text,approved,status,notes) values
('TFW-20261023-01','2026-10-23',('2026-11-11 20:00'::timestamp at time zone 'America/Toronto'),'Carousel','CAROUSEL',$c$2026-10-23_Carousel_TCF-Writing-Task-1$c$,'2026-10-23_Carousel_TCF-Writing-Task-1',array['https://raw.githubusercontent.com/thefrenchway2pr-ux/tfw2pr-media/main/media/2026-10-23/2026-10-23_Carousel_TCF-Writing-Task-1_01.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/thefrenchway2pr-ux/tfw2pr-media/main/media/2026-10-23/2026-10-23_Carousel_TCF-Writing-Task-1_02.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/thefrenchway2pr-ux/tfw2pr-media/main/media/2026-10-23/2026-10-23_Carousel_TCF-Writing-Task-1_03.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/thefrenchway2pr-ux/tfw2pr-media/main/media/2026-10-23/2026-10-23_Carousel_TCF-Writing-Task-1_04.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/thefrenchway2pr-ux/tfw2pr-media/main/media/2026-10-23/2026-10-23_Carousel_TCF-Writing-Task-1_05.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/thefrenchway2pr-ux/tfw2pr-media/main/media/2026-10-23/2026-10-23_Carousel_TCF-Writing-Task-1_06.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/thefrenchway2pr-ux/tfw2pr-media/main/media/2026-10-23/2026-10-23_Carousel_TCF-Writing-Task-1_07.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/thefrenchway2pr-ux/tfw2pr-media/main/media/2026-10-23/2026-10-23_Carousel_TCF-Writing-Task-1_08.jpg'],$c$Your friend is visiting Toronto in December and asks for advice. You have 60 to 120 words to answer. In French. That's TCF Canada writing, Task 1.

Task 1 is a short message to someone you know. It looks easy, so many candidates rush it: they skip a point of the prompt, switch between tu and vous, or write a list instead of a message. Swipe for the 4 steps.

A model answer (about 95 words):

« Salut Karim !

Super nouvelle, j'ai hâte de te voir à Toronto ! Pour les vêtements, il fait très froid en décembre, alors je te conseille d'apporter un bon manteau, une tuque et des bottes. Côté activités, tu devrais essayer le patin à glace à Nathan Phillips Square, c'est magnifique le soir. Il y a aussi un marché de Noël dans le Distillery District. Pour te déplacer, il vaut mieux prendre le métro : c'est simple et rapide. N'oublie pas d'acheter une carte Presto.

Écris-moi si tu as des questions. À très bientôt !

Priya »

10 expressions to save:
→ Salut Karim ! (Hi Karim!)
→ Merci pour ton message ! (Thanks for your message!)
→ J'ai hâte de te voir ! (I can't wait to see you!)
→ Je te conseille de + infinitive (I advise you to…)
→ Tu devrais + infinitive (You should…)
→ Il vaut mieux + infinitive (It's better to…)
→ N'oublie pas de + infinitive (Don't forget to…)
→ Côté activités, … (As for activities, …)
→ Écris-moi si tu as des questions. (Write to me if you have any questions.)
→ À très bientôt ! (See you very soon!)

Takeaway: one point of the prompt = one paragraph, one register from start to finish, and at least 3 different ways to give advice.

Quiz answers (slide 7): 1. de · 2. prendre · 3. ton

Want 3 real Canadian conversations and 10 exercises with answers on this? DM « PR » and I'll send you the practical guide.

