insert into public.social_posts (row_id,post_date,publish_at,content_type,ig_media_type,topic,asset_name,media_urls,caption,alt_text,approved,status,notes) values
('TFW-20261024-01','2026-10-24',('2026-11-12 20:00'::timestamp at time zone 'America/Toronto'),'Static','IMAGE',$c$2026-10-24_Static_Learn-French-in-Chunks$c$,'2026-10-24_Static_Learn-French-in-Chunks',array['https://raw.githubusercontent.com/thefrenchway2pr-ux/tfw2pr-media/main/media/2026-10-24/2026-10-24_Static_Learn-French-in-Chunks_01.jpg'],$c$You know the words. So why does your mind go blank when you need a full sentence in French?

Because you're building it word by word. Fluent speakers don't: they use ready-made blocks (chunks) like « j'ai besoin de » or « je viens de », then add the end of the sentence.

Study tip: learn each block WITH its little word (de or à). « J'ai du mal à » and « j'ai mal à » are not the same thing at all!

10 blocks to save:
→ J'ai besoin de parler plus souvent. (I need to speak more often.)
→ J'ai du mal à comprendre quand on parle vite. (I have trouble understanding when people speak fast.)
→ Je n'arrive pas à trouver mes mots. (I just can't find my words.)
→ Je suis en train de préparer le TEF. (I'm preparing for the TEF right now.)
→ Je viens de finir mon cours. (I've just finished my class.)
→ J'ai envie de sortir ce soir. (I feel like going out tonight.)
→ Je compte passer le TCF au printemps. (I'm planning to take the TCF in the spring.)
→ Ça me permet de pratiquer tous les jours. (It lets me practice every day.)
→ Je m'habitue à l'hiver canadien. (I'm getting used to the Canadian winter.)
→ Je suis sur le point de partir. (I'm about to leave.)

Takeaway: choose 3 blocks today. Write one true sentence about your life with each, then say them out loud 3 times. Tomorrow, use one in a real conversation.

Want to practice your blocks out loud with a teacher who corrects you on the spot? Book a trial class: the link is in my bio.

