('TFW-20261025-01','2026-10-25',('2026-11-13 20:00'::timestamp at time zone 'America/Toronto'),'Carousel','CAROUSEL',$c$2026-10-25_Carousel_Story-La-Maison-d-en-Face$c$,'2026-10-25_Carousel_Story-La-Maison-d-en-Face',array['https://raw.githubusercontent.com/thefrenchway2pr-ux/tfw2pr-media/main/media/2026-10-25/2026-10-25_Carousel_Story-La-Maison-d-en-Face_01.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/thefrenchway2pr-ux/tfw2pr-media/main/media/2026-10-25/2026-10-25_Carousel_Story-La-Maison-d-en-Face_02.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/thefrenchway2pr-ux/tfw2pr-media/main/media/2026-10-25/2026-10-25_Carousel_Story-La-Maison-d-en-Face_03.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/thefrenchway2pr-ux/tfw2pr-media/main/media/2026-10-25/2026-10-25_Carousel_Story-La-Maison-d-en-Face_04.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/thefrenchway2pr-ux/tfw2pr-media/main/media/2026-10-25/2026-10-25_Carousel_Story-La-Maison-d-en-Face_05.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/thefrenchway2pr-ux/tfw2pr-media/main/media/2026-10-25/2026-10-25_Carousel_Story-La-Maison-d-en-Face_06.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/thefrenchway2pr-ux/tfw2pr-media/main/media/2026-10-25/2026-10-25_Carousel_Story-La-Maison-d-en-Face_07.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/thefrenchway2pr-ux/tfw2pr-media/main/media/2026-10-25/2026-10-25_Carousel_Story-La-Maison-d-en-Face_08.jpg'],$c$9 p.m. Nobody lives in the house across the street. So why are two orange eyes shining in the window? Can you follow this suspense story in French? It's A1.

This mini story is written like the stories in our A1 suspense reader: short sentences, the present tense, and words you'll use with your neighbors in Canada. Swipe, read each part out loud, then answer the 3 questions on slide 7.

10 words from the story:
→ la fenêtre (the window): regarder par la fenêtre = to look out the window
→ en face (across the street): la maison d'en face
→ personne… ne (nobody): « Personne n'habite là. » No « pas » !
→ briller (to shine): les yeux brillent
→ bouger (to move): il ne bouge pas
→ frapper à la porte (to knock on the door)
→ ouvrir ≠ fermer (to open ≠ to close)
→ sourire (to smile): elle sourit
→ le voisin / la voisine (the neighbor, m. / f.)
→ la citrouille (the pumpkin)

Takeaway: underline the verbs. Regarde, s'allume, brillent, frappe, ouvre, sourit: they're all in the present tense. At A1, the present is enough to tell a whole story, so start telling yours.

Answers (no peeking):
1. Ravi habite à Laval.
2. Claire, sa nouvelle voisine.
3. Une citrouille pour l'Halloween ! The orange light is inside.

Did you guess the ending? Comment your 3 answers in French below. I reply to every one.

