insert into public.social_posts (row_id,post_date,publish_at,content_type,ig_media_type,topic,asset_name,media_urls,caption,alt_text,approved,status,notes) values
('TFW-20261026-01','2026-10-26',('2026-11-14 20:00'::timestamp at time zone 'America/Toronto'),'Static','IMAGE',$c$2026-10-26_Static_Reflexive-Verbs-Me-Te-Se$c$,'2026-10-26_Static_Reflexive-Verbs-Me-Te-Se',array['https://raw.githubusercontent.com/thefrenchway2pr-ux/tfw2pr-media/main/media/2026-10-26/2026-10-26_Static_Reflexive-Verbs-Me-Te-Se_01.jpg'],$c$« Je me souviens. » It's on every Québec license plate, and it's a perfect little lesson in French grammar.

Se souvenir (to remember) is a reflexive verb: it comes with a small pronoun that matches the subject. A very common mistake is using « se » for everyone. « Je se souviens » ❌ « Je me souviens » ✅

je me · tu te · il / elle / on se · nous nous · vous vous · ils / elles se
(me, te, se become m', t', s' before a vowel)

10 examples you'll use in Canada:
→ Je m'inscris à la bibliothèque. (I'm signing up at the library.)
→ Tu t'habitues à l'hiver ? (Are you getting used to the winter?)
→ Il se souvient de mon nom. (He remembers my name.)
→ Nous nous occupons des enfants le soir. (We look after the kids in the evening.)
→ Vous vous trompez de numéro. (You have the wrong number.)
→ Elles se parlent en français au travail. (They talk to each other in French at work.)
→ Je ne me souviens pas de mon mot de passe. (I don't remember my password.)
→ Je vais m'inscrire au cours du soir. (I'm going to sign up for the evening class.)
→ Dépêche-toi, l'autobus arrive ! (Hurry up, the bus is coming!)
→ On se voit demain ? (See you tomorrow?)

Watch the word order: in the negative, ne goes before the pronoun (je ne me souviens pas). With two verbs, the pronoun goes before the infinitive and still matches the subject (je vais m'inscrire, nous allons nous inscrire).

Takeaway: when the dictionary lists a verb as « se + verb », learn it as « je me… » and change the pronoun with every subject.

Want 3 real conversations (the library, the office, a wrong-number call) and 10 exercises with answers? DM « PR » and I'll send you the practical guide.

